==English==

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|grc}} {{term|sc=polytonic|Πύθων|tr=Puthōn||lang=grc}}, the name of the mythological enormous serpent at Delphi slain by Apollo, from {{term|sc=polytonic|Πυθώ|tr=Pūthō|lang=grc}}, the early name of Delphi, from {{term|sc=polytonic|πυθώ|tr=puthō||to rot, to decay|lang=grc}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{a|RP}} {{IPA|/ˈpaɪθən/}}, {{SAMPA|/paIT@n/}}
* {{a|US}} {{IPA|/ˈpaɪθɑːn/}}

===Noun===
'''python''' (''plural'' '''[[pythons]]''')

# A type of large [[constrict]]ing [[snake]].

